            "description": "Watch Willem II vs FC Volendam highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 20, 2026. The atmosphere was thick with anticipation as both sides took to the pitch for this crucial league encounter. With the fans creating a vibrant backdrop, the match promised to be a tactical battle where clinical finishing would prove to be the ultimate difference. Early Shocks and Volendam’s Clinical Edge On May 20, 2026 , the Eredivisie played host to a dramatic clash between Willem II and FC Volendam . The home side almost had the perfect start in the 2nd minute when Anthony Descotte struck the post, a sign of the frustration to come. FC Volendam clinicaly punished defensive lapses to take control. In the 13th minute, Bilal Ould-Chikh pounced on a mistake by Per van Loon to fire home with his left foot. The lead was doubled just five minutes later when Henk Veerman capitalized on an error from goalkeeper Thomas Didillon , clinicaly slotting the ball into the net to leave the home crowd in shock. Willem II Fightback and Woodwork Woes The second half saw a rejuvenated Willem II side looking to overhaul the deficit. Their persistence paid off in the 54th minute when Nick Doodeman connected with a Gijs Besselink assist to pull one back with a tidy right-footed finish. Momentum shifted toward the hosts as they dominated 55% of the possession in front of 15,500 spectators. However, luck was not on their side; in the 75th minute, Anthony Descotte incredibly hit the post for the second time in the match, missing a golden opportunity to level the scores. Late Drama and Defensive Resilience The closing stages were frantic as Willem II threw everything forward. Brandley Kuwas delivered a series of dangerous corners, but the FC Volendam defense, anchored by timely clearances from Yannick Leliendal , held firm. Tensions boiled over in stoppage time as Amine Et Taibi received a yellow card for a shirt-pull on Dave Kwakman . Despite the late pressure and a series of desperate attacks, FC Volendam managed to protect their slim lead until the final whistle, securing a vital away victory in a contest defined by clinical finishing and defensive grit.",
